    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01ec31c3_ff5c55a3",
        "filename": "ai/ai-review-agent-gemini-1.0.groovy",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1025452
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T11:40:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is cached: AiProvidersInfoCacheImpl keeps the getModels() result in the persistent `models` cache for 1 day, keyed by plugin. So the probes run at most once a day, not on every dropdown render; a full refresh measured ~2.2s (15 probes with the current catalog).\n\nSide note: because the cache is keyed by plugin rather than by API key, the key of whoever triggers the daily refresh decides the list for everyone, and Google decides availability per key (\"no longer available to new users\"). That was already true for the plain listing before this change; happy to look at it in the provider plugin separately.",
      "parentUuid": "953b926e_54071e3b",
      "revId": "70eddd659961ab67d23e57733eb3dc3d4d21dde2",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3754d542_b374c613",
        "filename": "ai/ai-review-agent-gemini-1.0.groovy",
